{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"OSS / BUILD-VS-REUSE CHECK (2026-08-14; pinned main SHAs)\n\nSurveyed popular active test-heavy projects: pytest-dev/pytest (14.4k stars, 68308aa), pypa/pip (10.2k, f399c371), python-poetry/poetry (92b74dc), and pre-commit/pre-commit (15.5k, 9767b6c). All four isolate mutable state into pytester/tmp_path/temp Git repos or mock Git and none runs source-checkout `git rev-parse HEAD` before and after every test. pip has an autouse isolate fixture that remaps HOME/config into tmpdir; Poetry uses autouse tmp working directories and a Git mock; pre-commit creates all mutable Git repos under temp fixtures; pytest uses pytester/temp paths and only lightweight autouse environment resets. This is 4/4 consensus for keeping source-checkout VCS subprocesses out of the per-test hot path, with no documented rejection.\n\nHowever, the implementation primitive does NOT have consensus. Poetry uses Dulwich Repo for in-process Git semantics; pip and pre-commit deliberately use Git CLI/rev-parse in their Git-facing code (1/3 library, 2/3 CLI). None of the four maintains the stricter per-test checkout-HEAD attribution guard rebar requires. Removing that guard would match their baseline but violates this ticket/session fidelity constraint. Adding Dulwich/pygit2/GitPython solely for two metadata reads is not supported by 2/3 consensus and adds install/import/dependency surface to every test job. Hand-parsing symbolic/loose/packed/worktree refs is likewise not an OSS-consensus practice and carries the plan-review advisory around pack-refs/reftable correctness.\n\nDecision under the standing rule: the direction (eliminate 26k-ish per-suite source Git process launches) is consensus-backed, but neither fidelity-preserving implementation option reaches the automatic-approval bar. No production/test code changed. Retain the measured candidate (~75s projected macOS wall saving; ~207 runner-s) for operator disposition while higher-confidence editor and mutation RCA work continues."},"env_id":"0993f6a8-7a6a-4707-a671-c5bbb2691444","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786747572943943001,"uuid":"5d4c56ad-fb23-4b1d-abfe-9a0443bf049d"}